.Dd August 23, 2026
.Dt MAC_DO_AUTO 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mac_do_auto
.Nd MAC policy for transparent privilege escalation by group membership
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To load the module at boot time, place the following line in
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mac_do_auto_load="YES"
.Ed
.Pp
To load it at runtime:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
kldload mac_do_auto
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
kernel module implements the
.Xr mac 4
framework's
.Fn mac_priv_grant
hook.
When standard file permissions deny an operation and the kernel checks
whether the process holds the required privilege,
.Nm
grants the privilege if the process credential includes membership in the
configured group (by default GID 0,
.Dq wheel ) .
The operation then succeeds as if the process were running as root,
without requiring
.Xr mdo 1 ,
.Xr sudo 8 ,
or
.Xr doas 1 .
.Pp
Privileges may be restricted to a subset (scope) and partitioned across
multiple groups by the
.Xr autodo-eventd 8
companion daemon.
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
The following variables are available under
.Dv security.mac.autodo :
.Bl -tag -width ".Va grant_count"
.It Va enabled
Enable or disable privilege grants globally (default: 1).
The host is governed by this knob; jails use the per-jail parameter
described below.
.It Va gid
GID whose members receive implicit privileges when no daemon-managed
policy is installed (default: 0, wheel).
.It Va log_grants
When non-zero, emit a rate-limited log line to the kernel message buffer
for each grant, and append audit events to the ring buffer described
below (default: 0).
.It Va grant_count
Read-only counter of privileges granted since module load.
.It Va scope
Privilege scope as a comma-separated list of categories, or
.Dq all
(default).
Categories:
.Li system , audit , cred , debug , jail , kld , proc , vfs , vm , dev ,
.Li net ,
and
.Li misc .
.El
.Sh DEVICE
The module creates
.Pa /dev/autodo
(mode 0640, root:wheel, single-open), which provides:
.Bl -bullet
.It
A ring buffer of audit events (fixed 48-byte records,
.Va struct autodo_event )
readable with
.Xr read 2 ,
.Xr poll 2 ,
and
.Xr kqueue 2 .
.It
The
.Xr ioctl 2
interface used by
.Xr autodo-eventd 8 :
.Dv AUTODO_SET_SCOPE / AUTODO_GET_SCOPE
(legacy single-group privilege bitmap),
.Dv AUTODO_SET_POLICY / AUTODO_GET_POLICY
(multi-group policy),
.Dv AUTODO_SET_PATHS / AUTODO_GET_PATHS
(path deny list), and
.Dv AUTODO_FLUSH
(discard pending events).
The programming interface is defined in
.Pa src/autodo.h .
.El
.Sh JAILS
The per-jail parameter
.Va mac.autodo
controls the policy inside jails:
.Dq disable
(default for new jails),
.Dq new
(enabled in this jail), or
.Dq inherit
(follow the parent jail).
Set with
.Xr jail 8
at creation time or via
.Xr jail 8
.Fl m .
.Sh PATH DENY LIST
An optional global list of path prefixes protects files from
autodo-elevated users.
Non-root members of managed groups are denied create, delete, rename,
mkdir, write, chmod/chown, and flag changes under the listed prefixes,
even though
.Nm
would otherwise grant them.
Root is exempt and reads are unaffected.
The list is empty by default and is managed by
.Xr autodo-eventd 8
from the
.Va deny
.Va paths
setting in
.Xr autodo.conf 5 .
.Pp
This is advisory footgun protection, not a security boundary:
relative paths from inside a denied directory, operations on file
descriptors opened before the deny, and path aliases (hard links)
are not covered.
Denials are logged, rate-limited, to the kernel message buffer.
.Sh UNLOADING
The module refuses to unload while
.Pa /dev/autodo
is open
.Pq Dv EBUSY .
Close the daemon and any other consumers before running
.Xr kldunload 8 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mac 4 ,
.Xr mac_bsdextended 4 ,
.Xr autodo.conf 5 ,
.Xr autodo-eventd 8 ,
.Xr kldload 8
